      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{x}-1?$",
      "worked_solution": "To obtain the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{x}-1,$ we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Reflect the graph in the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{x}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14258624/assets/19cba78ef000b6a44978f813f427cc709f2e711b39fdeca42c5b422c3596912e.png)\n\n- Translate the result down by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{x}-1.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14258624/assets/c36aea6e6fd29868721a9bac0f817ad2824636a844cc4d1a8ead33d296d384d3.png)",
